361
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:33,640
♪ I want to fall in love with you ♪

362
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:33,570
Mr. Xu?

363
00:25:33,660 --> 00:25:36,470
♪ No matter how many times I say
I love you ♪

364
00:25:36,490 --> 00:25:40,070
♪ Clouds, please drift a little closer ♪

365
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:39,440
My only childhood friend is my brother.

366
00:25:40,970 --> 00:25:45,870
♪ I could say it ten thousand times
and never tire ♪

367
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:46,610
You get one, too.

368
00:25:47,330 --> 00:25:48,790
Have fun together with me.

369
00:25:57,680 --> 00:26:00,950
♪ Practice the poem of love
time and again ♪

370
00:25:59,850 --> 00:26:00,920
You draw one, too!

371
00:26:00,980 --> 00:26:04,380
♪ Where should I begin
with these soft and low whispers? ♪

372
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:02,640
Draw what?

373
00:26:02,960 --> 00:26:04,480
Draw whatever you want.

374
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:07,540
♪ The moonlight is
gently cast upon your name ♪

375
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:11,760
♪ I look up,
and you're always there, so tenderly ♪

376
00:26:12,010 --> 00:26:14,460
♪ Through seasons of endless change ♪

377
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:17,120
♪ Through ceaseless tides
that ebb and flow ♪

378
00:26:18,840 --> 00:26:21,340
♪ Letting moments overlap ♪

379
00:26:21,370 --> 00:26:24,760
♪ As we feel the changes of seasons ♪

380
00:26:25,340 --> 00:26:28,910
♪ I'm just glad I was brave enough ♪

381
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,900
May I borrow your phone?

382
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:31,940
♪ To meet the moon ♪

383
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:34,640
♪ Gently, I pluck a piece of it ♪

384
00:26:34,670 --> 00:26:37,810
♪ And let loneliness fade away ♪

385
00:26:37,970 --> 00:26:42,130
♪ All I want is to be with you ♪

386
00:26:42,320 --> 00:26:45,190
♪ That's the only thing that matters ♪

387
00:26:45,300 --> 00:26:49,040
♪ Love gives us all ♪

388
00:26:49,060 --> 00:26:52,120
♪ Like the moon lighting up every night ♪

389
00:26:52,140 --> 00:26:52,960
♪ You know ♪

390
00:26:52,220 --> 00:26:53,790
Remember to send me the photos.

391
00:26:52,980 --> 00:26:56,220
♪ I want to fall in love with you ♪

392
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:54,700
Mm.

393
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:59,050
♪ No matter how many times I say
I love you ♪

394
00:26:59,070 --> 00:27:02,650
♪ Clouds, please drift a little closer ♪

395
00:27:00,070 --> 00:27:01,010
Today is the happiest day

396
00:27:01,010 --> 00:27:02,240
I've had this year.

397
00:27:03,550 --> 00:27:08,450
♪ I could say it ten thousand times
and never tire ♪

398
00:27:04,550 --> 00:27:05,880
The year isn't over yet.

399
00:27:07,110 --> 00:27:07,920
Then tell me.

400
00:27:08,540 --> 00:27:09,150
Do you remember

401
00:27:09,150 --> 00:27:11,010
what you did on this day last year?

402
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:15,290
Me neither.

403
00:27:15,870 --> 00:27:20,030
♪ All I want is to be with you ♪

404
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:16,350
But

405
00:27:16,350 --> 00:27:17,920
next year, I'll definitely remember

406
00:27:17,920 --> 00:27:20,050
what I did today.

407
00:27:20,090 --> 00:27:22,840
♪ That's the only thing that matters ♪

408
00:27:22,860 --> 00:27:26,810
♪ Love gives us all ♪

409
00:27:26,830 --> 00:27:29,890
♪ Like the moon lighting up every night ♪

410
00:27:29,910 --> 00:27:30,730
♪ You know ♪

411
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:33,990
♪ I want to fall in love with you ♪

412
00:27:34,010 --> 00:27:36,820
♪ No matter how many times I say
I love you ♪

413
00:27:36,850 --> 00:27:40,430
♪ Clouds, please drift a little closer ♪

414
00:27:41,320 --> 00:27:46,220
♪ I could say it ten thousand times
and never tire ♪

415
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,270
Thank you for seeing me home.

416
00:28:02,270 --> 00:28:02,740
Mm.

417
00:28:04,380 --> 00:28:05,910
Remember to take your meds.

418
00:28:06,350 --> 00:28:07,700
Mm, okay.

419
00:28:14,900 --> 00:28:15,900
Go back inside.

420
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:17,160
Mm.

421
00:28:21,810 --> 00:28:22,610
By the way...

422
00:28:23,530 --> 00:28:25,790
There's one more thing I want to tell you.

423
00:28:30,180 --> 00:28:30,980
Go ahead.

424
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:42,720
Is it something important?

425
00:28:44,050 --> 00:28:45,250
It's very important.

426
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,250
Actually...

427
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:58,090
A-Actually, I...

428
00:29:03,770 --> 00:29:05,030
I am the same age as you.

429
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:14,270
I-If you don't believe me,

430
00:29:14,270 --> 00:29:15,850
I can show you my ID card.

431
00:29:17,250 --> 00:29:18,050
I believe you.

432
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:26,960
What month were you born in?

433
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:28,400
February.

434
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:32,480
I'm only one month younger than you.

435
00:29:32,940 --> 00:29:33,880
So you don't have

436
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:36,140
to treat me as a junior
and take care of me.

437
00:29:38,070 --> 00:29:39,800
Then what should I treat you as?

438
00:29:41,180 --> 00:29:42,980
A... friend?

439
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:57,340
You freaked me out.

440
00:29:57,960 --> 00:29:59,960
Tangy, what are you doing here?

441
00:30:00,270 --> 00:30:01,610
Lili, you're back.

442
00:30:02,610 --> 00:30:04,740
Have you gotten better from your cold?

443
00:30:06,350 --> 00:30:07,240
Thanks to your medicine,

444
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:08,050
I'm much better now.

445
00:30:08,050 --> 00:30:08,980
What medicine?

446
00:30:09,460 --> 00:30:10,380
Cold medicine, of course!

447
00:30:10,380 --> 00:30:11,910
The one you left on my table.

448
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:13,110
I didn't do it.

449
00:30:13,250 --> 00:30:14,050
You didn't?

450
00:30:16,210 --> 00:30:17,160
Was it Fu Shize?

451
00:30:17,750 --> 00:30:19,280
Remember to take your meds.

452
00:30:25,460 --> 00:30:26,110
Did anything

453
00:30:26,110 --> 00:30:27,460
happen between you two?

454
00:30:27,510 --> 00:30:28,510
Come on, spill it.

455
00:30:29,420 --> 00:30:30,220
Well...

456
00:30:32,660 --> 00:30:33,570
Today, Mr. Qin

457
00:30:33,590 --> 00:30:35,750
made me work overtime deliberately, right?

458
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:37,550
And then Fu Shize stood up for me.

459
00:30:37,610 --> 00:30:39,680
He also went for a walk with me,

460
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:40,980
lit sparklers,

461
00:30:40,980 --> 00:30:42,570
and sent me back.

462
00:30:42,570 --> 00:30:43,660
Not bad!

463
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:45,220
What a rich itinerary!

464
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:50,010
So you came back so late

465
00:30:50,010 --> 00:30:51,460
because you went on a date?

466
00:30:51,460 --> 00:30:53,070
N-No, it doesn't count as a date.

467
00:30:53,070 --> 00:30:53,720
Um...

468
00:30:54,550 --> 00:30:56,050
A guy and a girl were alone together

469
00:30:56,050 --> 00:30:56,980
this late at night,

470
00:30:56,980 --> 00:30:58,050
lighting sparklers?

471
00:30:58,050 --> 00:30:59,780
What else could it be but a date?

472
00:31:00,250 --> 00:31:01,050
Tell me.

473
00:31:01,510 --> 00:31:02,840
How far have things gone

474
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,610
between you two now?

475
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,480
We've made it clear.

476
00:31:06,960 --> 00:31:07,680
We are now

477
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:09,270
officially friends!

478
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:11,750
Just friends?

479
00:31:13,320 --> 00:31:15,300
I've already made great strides.

480
00:31:15,320 --> 00:31:17,520
At least he no longer sees me as a junior.

481
00:31:17,590 --> 00:31:18,400
I'm already happy

482
00:31:18,400 --> 00:31:20,350
being friends with him.

483
00:31:20,510 --> 00:31:22,550
You're happy with so little!

484
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:26,200
There's a whole galaxy

485
00:31:26,310 --> 00:31:28,640
between "just friend" and "girlfriend."

486
00:31:31,010 --> 00:31:33,260
I've already done a 100-meter sprint.

487
00:31:33,290 --> 00:31:35,400
I should at least be allowed
to catch my breath.

488
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:36,250
No way.

489
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:38,290
You're at the starting line now,

490
00:31:38,290 --> 00:31:39,720
still so far from the finish line.

491
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:41,720
You must sprint with all your might.

492
00:31:41,810 --> 00:31:44,720
Love is about timing. You have to act
when there are good feelings,

493
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:46,900
turning a friend

494
00:31:47,090 --> 00:31:49,150
into a boyfriend as soon as possible.

495
00:31:50,750 --> 00:31:52,460
Should I court him then?

496
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:53,460
Yes, of course.

497
00:31:53,590 --> 00:31:54,720
You must pursue him.

498
00:31:55,180 --> 00:31:57,440
You're pursuing this moon in your heart.

499
00:31:58,330 --> 00:32:00,400
How high do you think my chances

500
00:32:00,400 --> 00:32:01,900
of success are?

501
00:32:02,090 --> 00:32:03,700
Probably about...

502
00:32:05,270 --> 00:32:06,440
0.1%.

503
00:32:06,770 --> 00:32:07,680
This low?

504
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:10,200
Forget it.

505
00:32:10,200 --> 00:32:11,590
I'm not going to embarrass myself.

506
00:32:11,590 --> 00:32:13,530
I'm happy just being friends with him.

507
00:32:13,530 --> 00:32:15,060
Let's just leave it at that.

508
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:16,620
No!

509
00:32:16,700 --> 00:32:18,560
How will you know if you don't try?

510
00:32:18,820 --> 00:32:19,620
By the way,

511
00:32:19,700 --> 00:32:20,680
didn't he say last time

512
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:22,740
that the crepe rolls you made
were really good?

513
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:24,240
How about you make some more for him?

514
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:25,070
I asked him about it,

515
00:32:25,070 --> 00:32:26,140
and he said no.

516
00:32:26,290 --> 00:32:27,950
He said no, so you just give up?

517
00:32:28,030 --> 00:32:29,480
If you just make them

518
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:30,790
and put them in front of him,

519
00:32:30,790 --> 00:32:31,920
could he refuse you?

520
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:33,980
You're so right.

521
00:32:33,980 --> 00:32:35,290
I'll make crepe rolls tomorrow

522
00:32:35,290 --> 00:32:36,490
and bring them to him.

523
00:32:36,900 --> 00:32:37,700
That's right.

524
00:32:37,980 --> 00:32:39,570
The way to a man's heart

525
00:32:39,570 --> 00:32:41,180
is through his stomach.

526
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:47,200
Enough about me.

527
00:32:47,270 --> 00:32:48,130
What about you?

528
00:32:48,530 --> 00:32:49,940
You give me advice every day,

529
00:32:49,940 --> 00:32:51,400
but are you dating anyone?

530
00:32:51,980 --> 00:32:53,640
You're not getting any younger.

531
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:55,500
It's time for you to date someone.

532
00:32:56,460 --> 00:32:58,920
What do you mean
I'm not getting any younger?

533
00:32:59,770 --> 00:33:01,180
I'm in my prime!

534
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:03,200
I'm just waiting to meet the right person

535
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:04,330
at the right time.

536
00:33:04,590 --> 00:33:06,590
I'd rather date no one
than settle for less, you know?

537
00:33:06,590 --> 00:33:08,200
You'd rather date no one
than settle for less.

538
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:08,810
Let's drop it.

539
00:33:08,810 --> 00:33:09,810
I'm heading home.

540
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:12,420
Rest early, huh?

541
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:42,200
Photo received.

542
00:33:51,610 --> 00:33:53,240
I had a great time today.

543
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:55,200
Get some good rest.

544
00:33:55,460 --> 00:33:56,120
Good night.

545
00:35:04,820 --> 00:35:07,280
Don't have iced coffee only
in the morning.

546
00:35:07,380 --> 00:35:09,640
Eat some breakfast to fill your stomach.

547
00:35:30,010 --> 00:35:31,380
Hello, anyone from Engineering?

548
00:35:31,380 --> 00:35:32,820
The expression tester is malfunctioning.

549
00:35:32,820 --> 00:35:33,960
Could someone from Engineering

550
00:35:33,960 --> 00:35:35,290
come over and repair it?

551
00:35:38,820 --> 00:35:39,550
Engineer Fu,

552
00:35:39,550 --> 00:35:41,550
the machine's screen is glitching.

553
00:35:41,590 --> 00:35:42,340
Let me check.

554
00:35:55,270 --> 00:35:56,270
You know what?

555
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:57,420
You made the right choice

556
00:35:57,420 --> 00:35:58,380
joining our skateboard club.

557
00:35:58,380 --> 00:35:59,090
Really?

558
00:35:59,090 --> 00:36:00,940
I've been skateboarding for 7 years.

559
00:36:00,940 --> 00:36:02,050
I'm really good at it.

560
00:36:02,050 --> 00:36:02,570
No way,

561
00:36:02,780 --> 00:36:03,860
I must figure out a way

562
00:36:03,860 --> 00:36:05,300
and not let someone else get to him first.

563
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:06,300
Feel free to ask me anytime

564
00:36:06,300 --> 00:36:07,650
if you have any questions.

565
00:36:07,650 --> 00:36:08,140
Great.

566
00:36:08,170 --> 00:36:09,010
Thank you, senior.

567
00:36:09,010 --> 00:36:10,210
That's so nice of you.

568
00:36:12,690 --> 00:36:14,090
His level is just average.

569
00:36:14,090 --> 00:36:15,890
Anyone who can skate can do that.

570
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,530
I am indeed average.

571
00:36:17,530 --> 00:36:18,090
But as long as you

572
00:36:18,090 --> 00:36:19,050
come to our skateboard club more often

573
00:36:19,050 --> 00:36:19,570
